\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Illustration, not computed from data. Two concept volumes in a story space and the trajectory of SCENE\_1's states in story order. $z_1$ and $z_2$ are two of the story space's $d$ dimensions; $\sigma _k$ marks the point of the story's $k$-th state. $\sigma _1$, a warm sunny day, lies in neither volume. $\sigma _2$, Michael and Sarah setting out for a walk, lies only in $B_{\text  {Michael}}$. $\sigma _3$, an unexpected knock at their door, and $\sigma _4$, Michael going down to check, lie in the overlap. $\sigma _5$, Sarah calling ``Who is it?'', and $\sigma _6$, no answer coming, lie only in $B_{\text  {surprise visitor}}$.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:story-space}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
